00:44:15.570 --> 00:44:18.920
but the big switching to
Trump is happening here

00:44:18.920 --> 00:44:21.340
where nobody, nobody lives here.

00:44:21.340 --> 00:44:24.210
Very few Clinton voters are not concerned,

00:44:24.210 --> 00:44:26.560
or not at all concerned about Coronavirus.

00:44:26.560 --> 00:44:29.330
And those are the people
who are switching to Trump.

00:44:29.330 --> 00:44:32.740
There's not a lot of switching
among people who are worried.

00:44:32.740 --> 00:44:35.910
And so I have done this
kind of switching analysis

00:44:35.910 --> 00:44:37.370
for a number of things.

00:44:37.370 --> 00:44:40.970
For racial attitudes, there's
some small effects there.

00:44:40.970 --> 00:44:44.450
For worried about losing
your job and the economy,

00:44:44.450 --> 00:44:46.160
there are some small effects there.

00:44:46.160 --> 00:44:49.940
But these COVID and
Coronavirus concern numbers

00:44:49.940 --> 00:44:52.100
are the biggest in terms of the things

00:44:52.100 --> 00:44:54.760
that are pushing people to switch.

00:44:54.760 --> 00:44:56.750
And so I will end there.

