00:54:12.910 --> 00:54:16.800
college, non-college, turns out if you are

00:54:16.800 --> 00:54:19.430
college in a college neighborhood,

00:54:19.430 --> 00:54:20.503
you are different than college

00:54:20.503 --> 00:54:22.133
in a non-college neighborhood.

00:54:23.612 --> 00:54:25.440
And vice versa, if you're non-college.

00:54:25.440 --> 00:54:27.550
If you're non-college
and you do manual work,

00:54:27.550 --> 00:54:30.400
you're way different than
if you're non-college

00:54:30.400 --> 00:54:33.913
and you are a physician's assistant.

00:54:35.263 --> 00:54:39.130
And so by thinking that
something as broad as non-college

00:54:39.130 --> 00:54:42.920
is a sufficient proxy for the division

00:54:42.920 --> 00:54:45.990
is sort of missing that the response bias

00:54:45.990 --> 00:54:48.350
isn't because you got a
college degree or not,

00:54:48.350 --> 00:54:51.820
it's all these other things
that add up to something else.

00:54:51.820 --> 00:54:53.910
